Mark the end of each startup phase, but only once the console exists

The first attempt printed after every phase, including TUNABLES, TIMEOUTS and
LOCKS.  Those run before the console is initialised, so the printf took the
kernel down before it could print anything at all -- the panel stayed on the
DarwinBoot handoff text and no kernel output appeared.

The token probe already carried this guard (subsystem >= STARTUP_SUB_KPRINTF);
apply the same one here.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -437,3 +437,6 @@ kernel_startup_initialize_upto(startup_subsystem_id_t upto)
 		startup_entry_cur = ++cur;
 	}
+	if (upto >= STARTUP_SUB_KPRINTF) {
+		printf("\nE%u", (unsigned)upto);
+	}
 	kernel_startup_log(upto);
